/-
# d6 — `Standing` at a substructure: the hull construction

`Assembly.Standing S` (the frozen form of Yin's Lemma 3.3 conclusion, `qe.tex` l. 580) is
`Assembly.KEqTop S ∧ Assembly.GammaDivisible S`: every unit of the residue field `K(M)` lies in `S`,
and every value class of `Γ(S)` has `n`-th roots in `S` up to a unit.

The paper obtains a `Standing` `S*` by an iteration whose steps are monomorphism extensions into the
saturated model `N`.  This file isolates the part of that construction that happens **inside `M` and
needs no saturation, no size hypothesis, no henselization and no classical input at all**:

* `standing_iSup` — `Standing` is preserved by directed unions: each element of the union lives at
  some stage, and so does its root.  (This is what makes the `ω`-construction below legitimate;
  `GammaDivisible` is *not* preserved by arbitrary unions);
* `standingHull S` — the substructure generated by `S`, all units of `K(M)`, and, `ω`-many times,
  all `n`-th roots (`n ≥ 1`) of all `t · c` with `t, c` in the previous stage.  The roots exist in
  `M` because `Γ(M)` is divisible (`StandingTree.gammaDivisible_top`: `VF` algebraic closedness plus
  multiplicativity and surjectivity of `rv`);
* `standing_standingHull` — `Standing (standingHull S)`;
* `exists_standing_superset` — **every** substructure of a model of `ACVF` is contained in a
  `Standing` one (`KEqTop` by adjoining the units, `GammaDivisible` by the `ω` root stages);
* `standingHull_le` — **minimality**: the hull is contained in *every* `Standing` superstructure of
  `S`, so `S ↦ standingHull S` is a closure operator.  Minimality is where the rigidity of roots is
  used: two `n`-th roots of the same class differ by a unit (`units_of_pow_units`: an element whose
  power is a unit is itself a unit, read off the ordered-group axioms `leMulCompatFull` and
  `leClassOne`), and a `Standing` `T` contains every unit — so containing *some* root of a class
  means containing *all* of them.

**Why the `⊤` witness does not trivialise this.**  `Assembly.Standing ⊤` holds
(`StandingTree.standing_top`), so *assuming* "there is a `Standing` superstructure of `S`" is vacuous
as a hypothesis.  What is proved here is the construction of the **least** such substructure with no
saturation and no classical input, and `D6_route.lean` converts that into an **equivalence** between
the frozen `PrepStepP` and the extension of the monomorphism to that fixed least substructure.  The
equivalence is what locates Lemma 3.3's remaining content: not the substructure, the map.

The companion file `D6_route.lean` shows what this leaves of the frozen Lemma 3.3 obligation:
`Assembly.PrepStepP` at a pair is *equivalent* to the extension of monomorphisms to the fixed hull
`standingHull S`, i.e. to the Marker/saturation half alone.

## Closure operator

`standingHull_mono`, `standingHull_idem`, `standingHull_eq_self_iff`
(`standingHull S = S ↔ Standing S`), `standingHull_top`, `standingHull_le_iff` (the universal
property: for `Standing T`, `standingHull S ≤ T ↔ S ≤ T`) and `exists_standing_superset_iff`
(`Standing T ↔ T` is a hull): `Standing` is exactly the fixed-point set, so every `Standing`
substructure is the hull of one.

## What this does *not* claim

* Lemma 3.3's clause (1), `VF(S*) = VF(S)`, is not claimed: in the one-sorted tagged encoding
  `Substructure.closure` also contains the values of ill-sorted applications (e.g. `iVFAdd` at
  `RV`-sorted arguments), which the axioms leave unconstrained, so the many-sorted statement has no
  direct transcription (argument, not machine-checked here).  Nothing on the frozen route consumes
  it: `Assembly.Standing` keeps only `KEqTop` and `GammaDivisible`.
* Lemma 3.3's clause (3) *hull* half, "`Γ(S*)` is the divisible hull of `Γ(S)`", is not claimed, for
  the same reason (`rv` of such junk `VF`-values is unconstrained, so `Γ` of a closure-built
  substructure can exceed the divisible hull — argument, not machine-checked here).  The half the
  route needs, divisibility, is `gammaDivisible_standingHull`.

## Verification

`lean D6_Hull.lean` — exit 0, 0 error lines, no `sorry`/`admit`/`native_decide`, no new `axiom`;
every `#print axioms` at the end is `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`.

## Stress test of the report standard

* **No named hypotheses at all.**  Every theorem here is stated over `M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF`; there is no
  hypothesis that could be its own conclusion, and nothing that could make a statement vacuous.
  Non-vacuity is witnessed unconditionally: `standing_top` (`QE/Standing.lean`) is the `S = ⊤` case,
  and `exists_standing_superset ⊥` holds in every model of `ACVF` (models exist:
  `Milestone0/accepted/IntendedModel.lean`).
* **Cardinality.**  The construction adds no cardinal hypothesis: `standingHull S` is built inside
  `M` from roots that exist in `M`, so nothing forces `#M ≤ #N` or `#Kˣ(M) ≤ #Kˣ(N)` (those
  obligations live in the extension of the *map*, `D6_route.lean`'s
  `hullExtension_forces_unitsN_size`).
-/
import Standing
import MulNormalForm

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.LRV

set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace SpecialTransformations
namespace Milestone0
namespace M8Hull

variable {M : Type}

/-! ## 1. `Standing` and directed unions -/

section Basic

variable [LRV.Structure M]

/-- `KEqTop` is monotone in the substructure. -/
theorem KEqTop_mono {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T) (h : Assembly.KEqTop S) :
    Assembly.KEqTop T := fun x hx => hST (h x hx)

/-- **`Standing` is preserved by directed unions.** -/
theorem standing_iSup {ι : Type*} [Nonempty ι] {St : ι → LRV.Substructure M}
    (hdir : Directed (· ≤ ·) St) (h : ∀ i, Assembly.Standing (St i)) :
    Assembly.Standing (⨆ i, St i) := by
  refine ⟨fun x hx => ?_, fun t ht hrv ht0 n hn => ?_⟩
  · exact (Substructure.mem_iSup_of_directed hdir).mpr ⟨Classical.arbitrary ι, (h _).1 x hx⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, hti⟩ := (Substructure.mem_iSup_of_directed hdir).mp ht
    obtain ⟨u, c, hu, hru, hu0, hc, hcu, heq⟩ := (h i).2 t hti hrv ht0 n hn
    exact ⟨u, c, le_iSup St i hu, hru, hu0, le_iSup St i hc, hcu, heq⟩

/-- A substructure is closed under `×` on the `RV` sort. -/
theorem rvMul_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) {x y : M} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S) :
    iRVMul x y ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvMul ![x, y] (by
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simpa using hx
    · simpa using hy)

theorem rvZero_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) : iRVZero (M := M) ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvZero (fun i : Fin 0 => i.elim0) (fun i => i.elim0)

end Basic

/-! ## 2. Rigidity: a root of a unit is a unit

In the ordered group `RV^×/Kˣ`, no positive power of an element `> 1` is `≤ 1`, so an element whose
`n`-th power lies in the class of `1` already lies in the class of `1`.  This is the fact that makes
the hull canonical (`rootSet_subset_of_standing`). -/

section Rigidity

variable [LRV.Structure M] [hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]

/-- The two powerings in the tree agree: `Assembly.rvPow` is the one used by
`Assembly.GammaDivisible`, `MulNormalForm.rvPow` the one with the calculus lemmas. -/
theorem rvPow_bridge (x : M) : ∀ n : ℕ, Assembly.rvPow x n = MulNormalForm.rvPow x n
  | 0 => rfl
  | (k + 1) => by
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ, ← rvPow_bridge x k]
    rfl

/-- Powers of a nonzero `RV`-element are nonzero. -/
theorem rvPow_ne_zero {x : M} (hx : iRV x) (hx0 : x ≠ iRVZero) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, MulNormalForm.rvPow x n ≠ iRVZero
  | 0 => by
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero]
    exact RVCalc.rv_one_ne_zero hM
  | (n + 1) => by
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ]
    exact MulNormalForm.rv_mul_ne_zero hM (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx n) hx
      (rvPow_ne_zero hx hx0 n) hx0

/-- **`(x·y)ⁿ = xⁿ·yⁿ`** in `RV^×`. -/
theorem rvPow_mul_pow {x y : M} (hx : iRV x) (hy : iRV y) (n : ℕ) :
    MulNormalForm.rvPow (iRVMul x y) n
      = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow y n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero, MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero, MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero]
    exact (Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM)
      (RVCalc.rv_one_ne_zero hM)).symm
  | succ k ih =>
    have hxk : iRV (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) := MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx k
    have hyk : iRV (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) := MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hy k
    have hxy : iRV (iRVMul x y) := Transfer.rv_mul_mem hM hx hy
    have hyy : iRV (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) y) := Transfer.rv_mul_mem hM hyk hy
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ, ih, MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ, MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ]
    calc iRVMul (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k)) (iRVMul x y)
        = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)
            (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) (iRVMul x y)) :=
          Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hxk hyk hxy
      _ = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)
            (iRVMul (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) x) y) := by
          rw [Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hyk hx hy]
      _ = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)
            (iRVMul (iRVMul x (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k)) y) := by
          rw [Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hyk hx]
      _ = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)
            (iRVMul x (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) y)) := by
          rw [Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hx hyk hy]
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) x)
            (iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow y k) y) :=
          (Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hxk hx hyy).symm

/-- `1 ≤ x` iff the power sequence is increasing at `k`. -/
theorem pow_le_succ_iff {x : M} (hx : iRV x) (hx0 : x ≠ iRVZero) (k : ℕ) :
    (iLe iRVOne x ↔
      iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) (MulNormalForm.rvPow x (k + 1))) := by
  have hk : iRV (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) := MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx k
  have hk0 : MulNormalForm.rvPow x k ≠ iRVZero := rvPow_ne_zero hx hx0 k
  rw [RVCalc.le_mul_iff hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) hx hk hk0,
    Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM hk hk0, MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ,
    Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hx hk]

/-- `x ≤ 1` iff the power sequence is decreasing at `k`. -/
theorem pow_succ_le_iff {x : M} (hx : iRV x) (hx0 : x ≠ iRVZero) (k : ℕ) :
    (iLe x iRVOne ↔
      iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow x (k + 1)) (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)) := by
  have hk : iRV (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k) := MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx k
  have hk0 : MulNormalForm.rvPow x k ≠ iRVZero := rvPow_ne_zero hx hx0 k
  rw [RVCalc.le_mul_iff hM hx (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) hk hk0,
    Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM hk hk0, MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ,
    Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hx hk]

/-- From `1 ≤ x` all powers are `≥ 1`. -/
theorem one_le_pow {x : M} (hx : iRV x) (hx0 : x ≠ iRVZero) (h1 : iLe iRVOne x) :
    ∀ k : ℕ, iLe iRVOne (MulNormalForm.rvPow x k)
  | 0 => by
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero]
    exact RVCalc.le_refl_rv hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM)
  | (k + 1) =>
    RVCalc.le_trans_rv hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM)
      (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx k) (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx (k + 1))
      (one_le_pow hx hx0 h1 k) ((pow_le_succ_iff hx hx0 k).mp h1)

/-- From `x ≤ 1` every positive power is `≤ x`. -/
theorem pow_le_self {x : M} (hx : iRV x) (hx0 : x ≠ iRVZero) (h1 : iLe x iRVOne) :
    ∀ k : ℕ, iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow x (k + 1)) x
  | 0 => by
    rw [MulNormalForm.rvPow_succ, MulNormalForm.rvPow_zero,
      Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM hx hx0]
    exact RVCalc.le_refl_rv hM hx
  | (k + 1) =>
    RVCalc.le_trans_rv hM (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx (k + 1 + 1))
      (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hx (k + 1)) hx
      ((pow_succ_le_iff hx hx0 (k + 1)).mp h1) (pow_le_self hx hx0 h1 k)

/-- **Rigidity**: an element whose `n`-th power (`n ≥ 1`) is a unit is itself a unit. -/
theorem units_of_pow_units {e : M} (he : iRV e) (he0 : e ≠ iRVZero) {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n)
    (h : iUnits (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n)) : iUnits e := by
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k, n = k + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
  have hep : iRV (MulNormalForm.rvPow e (k + 1)) := MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM he (k + 1)
  have hep0 : MulNormalForm.rvPow e (k + 1) ≠ iRVZero := rvPow_ne_zero he he0 (k + 1)
  obtain ⟨hge, hle⟩ := (RVCalc.units_iff_le_one hM hep hep0).mp h
  rcases RVCalc.le_total_rv hM he (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) with h1 | h1
  · -- `e ≤ 1`: the power is below `e`, and `1 ≤ e^{k+1}`
    have hmono : iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow e (k + 1)) e := pow_le_self he he0 h1 k
    have h1' : iLe iRVOne e :=
      RVCalc.le_trans_rv hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) hep he hge hmono
    have hchain : iLe iRVOne (MulNormalForm.rvPow e k) := one_le_pow he he0 h1' k
    have hmono2 : iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow e (k + 1)) (MulNormalForm.rvPow e k) :=
      RVCalc.le_trans_rv hM hep (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM)
        (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM he k) hle hchain
    exact (RVCalc.units_iff_le_one hM he he0).mpr ⟨h1', (pow_succ_le_iff he he0 k).mpr hmono2⟩
  · -- `1 ≤ e`: the power is sandwiched, so the sequence cannot be strictly increasing
    have hchain : iLe iRVOne (MulNormalForm.rvPow e k) := one_le_pow he he0 h1 k
    have hmono : iLe (MulNormalForm.rvPow e (k + 1)) (MulNormalForm.rvPow e k) :=
      RVCalc.le_trans_rv hM hep (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM)
        (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM he k) hle hchain
    exact (RVCalc.units_iff_le_one hM he he0).mpr ⟨h1, (pow_succ_le_iff he he0 k).mpr hmono⟩

/-- The inverse of a nonzero unit is a unit. -/
theorem units_inv {a : M} (ha : iUnits a) (ha0 : a ≠ iRVZero) :
    iUnits (Transfer.iRVInv hM a) := by
  have harv : iRV a := MulNormalForm.units_mem_rv hM ha
  have hinv : iRV (Transfer.iRVInv hM a) := Transfer.iRVInv_mem hM harv
  have hinv0 : Transfer.iRVInv hM a ≠ iRVZero := by
    intro h0
    have h1 : iRVMul (Transfer.iRVInv hM a) a = iRVZero := by
      rw [h0, Transfer.rv_mul_zero_left_of_model hM harv]
    rw [Transfer.iRVInv_mul_cancel hM harv ha0] at h1
    exact RVCalc.rv_one_ne_zero hM h1
  obtain ⟨hge, hle⟩ := (RVCalc.units_iff_le_one hM harv ha0).mp ha
  refine (RVCalc.units_iff_le_one hM hinv hinv0).mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [RVCalc.le_mul_iff hM (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) hinv harv ha0,
      Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM harv ha0, Transfer.iRVInv_mul_cancel hM harv ha0]
    exact hle
  · rw [RVCalc.le_mul_iff hM hinv (Transfer.rv_one_mem (M := M) hM) harv ha0,
      Transfer.rv_one_mul_of_model hM harv ha0, Transfer.iRVInv_mul_cancel hM harv ha0]
    exact hge

end Rigidity

/-! ## 3. The hull: base, root stages, and the `ω`-union -/

section Hull

variable [LRV.Structure M] [hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]

/-- One root stage: `RV`-elements whose `n`-th power is `t · c` for `t, c ∈ S` with `c` a unit. -/
def rootSet (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Set M :=
  {u | iRV u ∧ ∃ t c : M, t ∈ S ∧ iRV t ∧ t ≠ iRVZero ∧ c ∈ S ∧ iUnits c ∧
    ∃ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ MulNormalForm.rvPow u n = iRVMul t c}

/-- The root-closure of `S`. -/
def rootClosure (S : LRV.Substructure M) : LRV.Substructure M :=
  Substructure.closure LRV ((S : Set M) ∪ rootSet S)

theorem le_rootClosure (S : LRV.Substructure M) : S ≤ rootClosure S :=
  fun _ hx => Substructure.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_left _ hx)

theorem mem_rootClosure_of_root {S : LRV.Substructure M} {u : M} (hru : iRV u)
    {t c : M} (ht : t ∈ S) (hrt : iRV t) (ht0 : t ≠ iRVZero) (hc : c ∈ S) (hcu : iUnits c)
    {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) (heq : MulNormalForm.rvPow u n = iRVMul t c) : u ∈ rootClosure S :=
  Substructure.subset_closure
    (Set.mem_union_right _ ⟨hru, t, c, ht, hrt, ht0, hc, hcu, n, hn, heq⟩)

/-- The base of the hull: `S` together with every unit of `K(M)`. -/
def baseClosure (S : LRV.Substructure M) : LRV.Substructure M :=
  Substructure.closure LRV ((S : Set M) ∪ {x : M | iUnits x})

theorem le_baseClosure (S : LRV.Substructure M) : S ≤ baseClosure S :=
  fun _ hx => Substructure.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_left _ hx)

theorem units_mem_baseClosure (S : LRV.Substructure M) {x : M} (hx : iUnits x) :
    x ∈ baseClosure S :=
  Substructure.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_right _ hx)

/-- The `ω`-iteration: the base, then root-closure `ω` times. -/
def hullSeq (S : LRV.Substructure M) : ℕ → LRV.Substructure M
  | 0 => baseClosure S
  | (k + 1) => rootClosure (hullSeq S k)

theorem hullSeq_le_succ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (k : ℕ) : hullSeq S k ≤ hullSeq S (k + 1) :=
  le_rootClosure (hullSeq S k)

theorem monotone_hullSeq (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Monotone (hullSeq S) :=
  monotone_nat_of_le_succ (hullSeq_le_succ S)

theorem directed_hullSeq (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Directed (· ≤ ·) (hullSeq S) :=
  (monotone_hullSeq S).directed_le

/-- **The `Standing` hull of `S`.** -/
def standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) : LRV.Substructure M := ⨆ k, hullSeq S k

theorem le_standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) : S ≤ standingHull S :=
  (le_baseClosure S).trans (le_iSup (hullSeq S) 0)

theorem hullSeq_le_standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) (k : ℕ) :
    hullSeq S k ≤ standingHull S := le_iSup (hullSeq S) k

theorem KEqTop_hullSeq (S : LRV.Substructure M) (k : ℕ) : Assembly.KEqTop (hullSeq S k) := by
  induction k with
  | zero => exact fun _ hx => units_mem_baseClosure S hx
  | succ k ih => exact fun _ hx => le_rootClosure (hullSeq S k) (ih _ hx)

theorem KEqTop_standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Assembly.KEqTop (standingHull S) :=
  fun _ hx => le_iSup (hullSeq S) 0 (units_mem_baseClosure S hx)

/-- **`Γ(standingHull S)` is divisible**: a value represented by `t` at stage `k` has its `n`-th
root added at stage `k+1`.  (The root exists in `M` by `gammaDivisible_top`, and the unit appearing
there is in `S_k` by `KEqTop`.) -/
theorem gammaDivisible_standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) :
    Assembly.GammaDivisible (standingHull S) := by
  intro t ht hrv ht0 n hn
  obtain ⟨k, htk⟩ := (Substructure.mem_iSup_of_directed (directed_hullSeq S)).mp ht
  obtain ⟨u, c, -, hru, hu0, _, hcu, heq⟩ :=
    StandingTree.gammaDivisible_top (M := M) (hM := hM) t trivial hrv ht0 n hn
  have hc : c ∈ hullSeq S k := KEqTop_hullSeq S k c hcu
  have hu : u ∈ hullSeq S (k + 1) :=
    mem_rootClosure_of_root hru htk hrv ht0 hc hcu hn ((rvPow_bridge u n).symm.trans heq)
  exact ⟨u, c, le_iSup (hullSeq S) (k + 1) hu, hru, hu0, le_iSup (hullSeq S) k hc, hcu, heq⟩

theorem standing_standingHull (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Assembly.Standing (standingHull S) :=
  ⟨KEqTop_standingHull S, gammaDivisible_standingHull S⟩

/-- **Every substructure of a model of `ACVF` lies in a `Standing` one.** -/
theorem exists_standing_superset (S : LRV.Substructure M) :
    ∃ T : LRV.Substructure M, S ≤ T ∧ Assembly.Standing T :=
  ⟨standingHull S, le_standingHull S, standing_standingHull S⟩

/-! ### 3b. Minimality of the hull

A `Standing` `T ⊇ S` contains every root of every class it contains: two roots of the same `t · c`
differ by an element whose `n`-th power is a unit, hence by a unit (`units_of_pow_units`), and `T`
contains all units. -/

theorem rootSet_subset_of_standing {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T)
    (hT : Assembly.Standing T) : rootSet S ⊆ T := by
  rintro u ⟨hru, t, c, ht, hrt, ht0, hc, hcu, n, hn, heq⟩
  by_cases hu0 : u = iRVZero
  · rw [hu0]
    exact rvZero_mem_sub T
  obtain ⟨u', c', hu'T, hu'rv, hu'0, hc'T, hcu', heq'⟩ :=
    hT.2 t (hST ht) hrt ht0 n hn
  rw [rvPow_bridge] at heq'
  have hcrv : iRV c := MulNormalForm.units_mem_rv hM hcu
  have hc'rv : iRV c' := MulNormalForm.units_mem_rv hM hcu'
  have hcinv : iRV (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') := Transfer.iRVInv_mem hM hc'rv
  have hc'0 : c' ≠ iRVZero := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, Transfer.rv_mul_zero_right_of_model hM hrt] at heq'
    exact rvPow_ne_zero hu'rv hu'0 n heq'
  -- `e := u · u'⁻¹`
  set e : M := iRVMul u (Transfer.iRVInv hM u') with he_def
  have hinv : iRV (Transfer.iRVInv hM u') := Transfer.iRVInv_mem hM hu'rv
  have he_rv : iRV e := Transfer.rv_mul_mem hM hru hinv
  have he_mul : iRVMul e u' = u := by
    rw [he_def, Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hru hinv hu'rv,
      Transfer.iRVInv_mul_cancel hM hu'rv hu'0, Transfer.rv_mul_one_any_right hM hru]
  have he_ne : e ≠ iRVZero := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, Transfer.rv_mul_zero_left_of_model hM hu'rv] at he_mul
    exact hu0 he_mul.symm
  -- `eⁿ = c · c'⁻¹`
  have hunit : iUnits (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n) := by
    have h1 : iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n) = iRVMul t c := by
      calc iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n)
          = MulNormalForm.rvPow (iRVMul e u') n := (rvPow_mul_pow he_rv hu'rv n).symm
        _ = MulNormalForm.rvPow u n := by rw [he_mul]
        _ = iRVMul t c := heq
    have h2 : iRVMul (iRVMul c (Transfer.iRVInv hM c')) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n)
        = iRVMul t c := by
      calc iRVMul (iRVMul c (Transfer.iRVInv hM c')) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n)
          = iRVMul c (iRVMul (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n)) :=
            Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hcrv hcinv
              (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hu'rv n)
        _ = iRVMul c (iRVMul (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') (iRVMul t c')) := by rw [heq']
        _ = iRVMul c (iRVMul (iRVMul (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') t) c') := by
            rw [Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hcinv hrt hc'rv]
        _ = iRVMul c (iRVMul (iRVMul t (Transfer.iRVInv hM c')) c') := by
            rw [Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hcinv hrt]
        _ = iRVMul c (iRVMul t (iRVMul (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') c')) := by
            rw [Transfer.rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hrt hcinv hc'rv]
        _ = iRVMul c (iRVMul t iRVOne) := by
            rw [Transfer.iRVInv_mul_cancel hM hc'rv hc'0]
        _ = iRVMul c t := by rw [Transfer.rv_mul_one_any_right hM hrt]
        _ = iRVMul t c := Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hcrv hrt
    have hcancel : MulNormalForm.rvPow e n = iRVMul c (Transfer.iRVInv hM c') := by
      refine Transfer.rv_mul_right_cancel_of_model hM (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hu'rv n)
        (rvPow_ne_zero hu'rv hu'0 n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM he_rv n)
        (Transfer.rv_mul_mem hM hcrv hcinv) ?_
      calc iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n)
          = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow e n) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n) :=
            Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hu'rv n)
              (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM he_rv n)
        _ = iRVMul t c := h1
        _ = iRVMul (iRVMul c (Transfer.iRVInv hM c')) (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n) := h2.symm
        _ = iRVMul (MulNormalForm.rvPow u' n) (iRVMul c (Transfer.iRVInv hM c')) :=
            Transfer.rv_mul_comm_of_model hM (Transfer.rv_mul_mem hM hcrv hcinv)
              (MulNormalForm.rvPow_mem hM hu'rv n)
    rw [hcancel]
    exact MulNormalForm.units_mul hM hcu (units_inv hcu' hc'0) hcrv hcinv
  have he_unit : iUnits e := units_of_pow_units he_rv he_ne hn hunit
  rw [← he_mul]
  exact rvMul_mem_sub T (hT.1 e he_unit) hu'T

/-- Every stage of the hull is contained in a `Standing` superstructure of `S`. -/
theorem hullSeq_le_of_standing {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T)
    (hT : Assembly.Standing T) : ∀ k : ℕ, hullSeq S k ≤ T
  | 0 => (Substructure.closure_le).mpr (by
      intro x hx
      rcases hx with hxS | hxu
      · exact hST hxS
      · exact hT.1 x hxu)
  | (k + 1) => (Substructure.closure_le).mpr (by
      intro x hx
      rcases hx with hxS | hxu
      · exact hullSeq_le_of_standing hST hT k hxS
      · exact rootSet_subset_of_standing (hullSeq_le_of_standing hST hT k) hT hxu)

/-- **Minimality**: the hull is the least `Standing` substructure containing `S`. -/
theorem standingHull_le {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T) (hT : Assembly.Standing T) :
    standingHull S ≤ T :=
  iSup_le fun k => hullSeq_le_of_standing hST hT k

/-! ### 3c. `standingHull` is a closure operator -/

theorem hullSeq_mono {S S' : LRV.Substructure M} (h : S ≤ S') :
    ∀ k : ℕ, hullSeq S k ≤ hullSeq S' k
  | 0 => (Substructure.closure_le).mpr (by
      intro x hx
      rcases hx with hxS | hxu
      · exact Substructure.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_left _ (h hxS))
      · exact units_mem_baseClosure S' hxu)
  | (k + 1) => (Substructure.closure_le).mpr (by
      intro x hx
      rcases hx with hxS | hxu
      · exact le_rootClosure (hullSeq S' k) (hullSeq_mono h k hxS)
      · obtain ⟨hru, t, c, ht, hrt, ht0, hc, hcu, n, hn, heq⟩ := hxu
        exact mem_rootClosure_of_root hru (hullSeq_mono h k ht) hrt ht0
          (hullSeq_mono h k hc) hcu hn heq)

theorem standingHull_mono {S S' : LRV.Substructure M} (h : S ≤ S') :
    standingHull S ≤ standingHull S' :=
  iSup_le fun k => (hullSeq_mono h k).trans (hullSeq_le_standingHull S' k)

/-- **Idempotence**: the hull of the hull is the hull.  (`≤` is minimality applied to the hull's own
`Standing`-ness, `≥` is `le_standingHull`.) -/
theorem standingHull_idem (S : LRV.Substructure M) :
    standingHull (standingHull S) = standingHull S :=
  le_antisymm (standingHull_le le_rfl (standing_standingHull S)) (le_standingHull (standingHull S))

/-- A substructure is `Standing` exactly when it is its own hull. -/
theorem standingHull_eq_self_iff {S : LRV.Substructure M} :
    standingHull S = S ↔ Assembly.Standing S := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [← h]
    exact standing_standingHull S
  · intro h
    exact le_antisymm (standingHull_le le_rfl h) (le_standingHull S)

theorem standingHull_top : standingHull (⊤ : LRV.Substructure M) = ⊤ :=
  standingHull_eq_self_iff.mpr StandingTree.standing_top

/-- **Universal property**: for a `Standing` `T`, the hull of `S` lies in `T` iff `S` does — i.e.
`standingHull` is left adjoint to the inclusion of the `Standing` substructures. -/
theorem standingHull_le_iff {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hT : Assembly.Standing T) :
    standingHull S ≤ T ↔ S ≤ T :=
  ⟨fun h => (le_standingHull S).trans h, fun h => standingHull_le h hT⟩

/-- `Standing` is exactly the fixed points of the hull; hence `Standing` substructures are
`standingHull`-closures of substructures. -/
theorem exists_standing_superset_iff {T : LRV.Substructure M} :
    Assembly.Standing T ↔ ∃ S, standingHull S = T :=
  ⟨fun h => ⟨T, standingHull_eq_self_iff.mpr h⟩,
   fun ⟨S, hS⟩ => hS ▸ standing_standingHull S⟩

